-- title:
--   Inertia moves prime-to-p torsion into the toric subgroup
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and $M \neq 0$ with $p \mid M$ but $p^2 \nmid M$, and a subgroup $H \leq (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$ containing every unit that reduces to $1$ in $(\mathbb{Z}/(M/p))^{\times}$. Assume the $q$-expansion `jqModC` of $j$ lies in the field `qExpFunctionFieldC` generated over $\mathbb{Q}$ by the integral form ratios for $\mathrm{SL}(2,\mathbb{Z})$, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a Deligne–Rapoport model datum `XHDRModelAtP` for $X_H(M)$ over $R_p$ at $p$. Let $\theta$ be an $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-algebra automorphism of the geometric function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\cdot F(\Gamma_H(M))$ (`xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, an intermediate field of Laurent series) which, on elements whose Laurent series come from level $M/p$ with group `infSubgroup p M H hpM`, acts by $q \mapsto q^{p}$ (the substitution `qExpand` by $p$); assume further that the automorphism $\mathfrak{X}.w$ induces $\theta$ on places, in the sense that whenever two $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points $y, y'$ of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ over the base satisfy $y'$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$, the first projection and $\mathfrak{X}.w$ equals $y$ followed by $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ and the first projection, the associated places satisfy $\mathrm{pointEquivPlace}(y') = \mathrm{SemilinearAut.ofAlgAut}(\theta) \cdot \mathrm{pointEquivPlace}(y)$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ with $p$ a nonunit of $A$ and with algebraically closed residue field of characteristic $p$, let $\Lambda$ be level data and $O$ a `JHNeronObjectAtP` over $\Lambda$, and assume the designation consisting of $O.G$, $O.g$ and the unit section of $O.L$ represents the relative Picard functor of the two-chart integral model `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj`, rigidified along $\mathfrak{X}.\varepsilon_{\inf}$ and cut out by fibrewise algebraic equivalence to zero (`algEquivZeroCut`). Then for every $m$ coprime to $p$, every $\sigma$ in the inertia subgroup attached to $A$ over $\mathbb{Q}$ (the image of the inertia subgroup inside the decomposition group in $\mathrm{Aut}_{\mathbb{Q}}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}})$), and every $x$ in the $m$-torsion of $\mathrm{Pic}^{0}$ of the geometric function field, the difference $\sigma \cdot x - x$ lies in $O.\mathrm{toricPts}\,m$, the subgroup of $J_H(M)$ generated by the range of $O.\mathrm{toricPoint}\,m$.
--
--   This is Grothendieck's orthogonality statement for the modular Jacobian $J_H(M)$ at a prime of multiplicative reduction: inertia acts unipotently of level two on prime-to-$p$ torsion, and $\sigma - 1$ takes such torsion into the toric part of the Néron model. It is used in the computation of the action of $\mathrm{Gal}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ on torsion via Hecke and diamond operators at $p$, and in the identification of the multiplicative part of the Tate module with a space of polar differentials.
